 "comment": "tds_payees buckets: a voucher with a Purchase Accounts or Sales Accounts line puts the mapped expense line's own amount (not the supplier's credit) in the goods-invoice bucket for each nature present, with no per-payee finding however large; a cash, bank or overdraft credit is the payee-not-named bucket, which does produce a finding over the limit. The goods bucket sums the mapped lines' SIGNED amounts: a credit-side freight line on a sales invoice lowers it, so the 194C bucket is negative here (pins signed, not absolute).",
